WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.262 --> 00:00:12.836
In this walkthrough, we create a new page from the Pages workspace and look at the required fields before saving.

2
00:00:12.836 --> 00:00:26.283
This is useful because almost every content task starts by finding the right place in the page tree and understanding whether the page should stay as a draft or be published.

3
00:00:26.283 --> 00:00:35.174
Open the Pages workspace and wait for the page tree to load.

4
00:00:35.174 --> 00:00:40.906
Click the add root page button to start a new site tree.

5
00:00:40.906 --> 00:00:45.942
The root page form asks for the key fields before anything is saved.

6
00:00:45.942 --> 00:00:55.195
Type a clear page title. The title helps editors recognize the new site tree.

7
00:00:55.195 --> 00:01:01.969
Enter the hostname where the root page should answer.

8
00:01:01.969 --> 00:01:08.277
Keep the page unpublished while you are still preparing content.

9
00:01:08.277 --> 00:01:15.888
For this walkthrough we cancel instead of creating demo content on the server.

10
00:01:15.888 --> 00:01:24.745
Use search to find existing pages before editing or adding more content.

11
00:01:24.745 --> 00:01:32.489
Refresh the page tree after changes or when collaborating with other editors.

12
00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:45.543
After this walkthrough, you should know where to start a new page, which fields matter first, and why it is safer to keep new work unpublished until the content is ready.
